<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>Plex Discord Bot - Plex Setup</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">
</head>
<body>
  <nav>
    <a href="/">Dashboard</a>
    <a href="/plex-setup">Plex Setup</a>
    <a href="/logout">Logout</a>
  </nav>
  <main>
    <h1>Plex Server Setup</h1>
    
    <% if (typeof success !== 'undefined' && success) { %>
      <div class="success"><%= success %></div>
    <% } %>
    
    <% if (typeof error !== 'undefined' && error) { %>
      <div class="error"><%= error %></div>
    <% } %>
    
    <h2>Step 1: Get Your Plex Token</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Go to <a href="https://plex.tv/settings" target="_blank">Plex Settings</a></li>
      <li>Click on your profile name in the top right</li>
      <li>Click "Account"</li>
      <li>Find "Authentication Token" and click "Show"</li>
      <li>Copy the token</li>
    </ol>
    
    <h2>Step 2: Find Your Plex Server URL</h2>
    <p>If your Plex server is on the same machine as this bot, use: <code>http://localhost:32400</code></p>
    <p>If it's on a different machine, use: <code>http://server-ip:32400</code></p>
    
    <h2>Step 3: Enter Your Credentials</h2>
    <form action="/plex-setup" method="POST">
      <label>Plex Server URL:</label>
      <input type="text" name="baseUrl" value="http://localhost:32400" placeholder="http://localhost:32400" required>
      
      <label>Plex Token:</label>
      <input type="password" name="token" placeholder="Your Plex authentication token" required>
      
      <button type="submit">Save and Test Connection</button>
    </form>
    
    <h3>Or use Plex OAuth</h3>
    <p>Instead of manually entering a token, you can authenticate directly through Plex:</p>
    <a href="/plex-oauth" class="btn">Connect with Plex OAuth</a>
  </main>
</body>
</html>